<div class="art-head"><div><div class="up" style="color:#8A8A8A">Beauty · Skincare · Melumé</div><h1 class="hd">Melumé Skincare Review: What I Actually Use</h1><p class="serif stand">I first tried Melumé in April 2024. My skin is normal but tends towards dryness, so I look for hydration, nourishment and care that supports my skin barrier.</p><div class="hand" style="transform:rotate(-2deg);font-size:34px;margin-top:10px">by Anna, from my own skin</div></div>
<div class="img art-hero"><img src="/img/mel-hero-l.webp" alt="Anna at the start of the Melumé video"></div></div></section>
<section class="p art-grid"><div class="art-body">

<p>Here’s what I actually use, the three products I keep finishing, and where the rest fits.</p>
<h2>At a glance</h2>
<ul>
<li>01 The 8HA pair Serum and cream</li>
<li>02 Lip balm All day</li>
<li>03 Evening Niacinamide, peptide</li>
<li>04 Occasional Peel and mask</li>
<li>05 Where I’d start My three</li>
</ul>
<h2>How I started</h2>
<p>Melumé found me on Instagram and wrote to me by email, and offered me three products of my choice. I picked Daily Hydra Lock Resurface Essence, the water-free Niacinamide Galactomyces Serum and Super C-Cream. The ingredient lists caught my eye, and the niacinamide serum made me most curious. What I reach for most today turned out to be a different little group.</p>
<div class="figrow"><figure class="fig"><img src="/img/mel-serum-8ha-l.webp" alt="A hand holding a blue dropper bottle of Melumé Hydrating Serum 8HA." loading="lazy"><figcaption>Hydrating Serum 8HA, one of my most-used products.</figcaption></figure><figure class="fig"><img src="/img/mel-cream-8ha-l.webp" alt="A hand holding a blue jar of Melumé Hydrating Cream 8HA with a white lid." loading="lazy"><figcaption>The Hydrating Cream 8HA I use throughout the year.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h2>Hydrating Serum 8HA and Hydrating Cream 8HA</h2>
<p>Everyday favourites.</p>
<p>I use them throughout the year, often in both my morning and evening skincare, and they’re among the products I finish most regularly. I reach for this pair when hydration and keeping my skin comfortable are the priority.</p>
<ProductFacts title="Hydrating Cream 8HA, at a glance" img="/img/mel-cream-8ha-l.webp" alt="A hand holding a blue jar of Melumé Hydrating Cream 8HA." pos="40% 50%" rows={[['Good for','Normal to dry skin, like mine'],['I use it','Morning and evening, all year'],['Why I reach for it','Hydration and keeping my skin comfortable'],['Pairs with','Hydrating Serum 8HA']]}/>
<figure class="fig"><img src="/img/mel-lip-l.webp" alt="A hand holding a jar of Melumé Maxi-Lip Filler Balm." loading="lazy"><figcaption>My frequently used Glossy Lip Line Eraser Maxi-Lip Filler Balm.</figcaption></figure>
<h2>Maxi-Lip Filler Balm</h2>
<p>People often ask what I’m wearing.</p>
<p>It keeps my lips moisturised for a long time without feeling sticky, and I like the slightly fuller look it gives them. With a lip pencil, this balm can be my whole lip combination.</p>
<div class="figrow"><figure class="fig"><img src="/img/mel-niacinamide-l.webp" alt="A hand holding a bottle of Melumé Water-free Niacinamide Galactomyces Serum with a black dropper." loading="lazy"><figcaption>The niacinamide serum was one of my first three Melumé products.</figcaption></figure><figure class="fig"><img src="/img/mel-peptide-l.webp" alt="A hand holding a pink tube of Melumé Power Peptide Micro Emulsion." loading="lazy"><figcaption>Power Peptide Micro Emulsion has a targeted place in my evening care.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h2>Evening: niacinamide and peptide</h2>
<p>Kept simple, with one targeted step.</p>
<p>I still use the niacinamide serum quite often, usually in the evening. I tend to follow it with a simple moisturiser, or one I choose for barrier support. Melumé <a href="https://www.melume-skinscience.com/products/niacinamide-serum" target="_blank" rel="noopener">lists 10% niacinamide in it</a> ; the water-free formula is what made me curious in the first place.</p>
<ProductInside img="/img/mel-niacinamide-l.webp" alt="Melumé Water-free Niacinamide Galactomyces Serum with a black dropper." pos="50% 45%" intro="Water-free, so it takes just 2–3 drops. These are the key ingredients on Melumé’s official page." items={[['10% niacinamide','The brand says it helps dark spots, post-acne discoloration and redness, and reduces sebum production and pore size.'],['80% galactomyces ferment filtrate','A yeast ferment that the brand says delivers nutrients, increases skin moisture and has an exfoliating effect.'],['Tranexamic acid','Described by the brand as fading stubborn dark spots and helping reduce sensitivity-induced redness.']]} also="snow mushroom, vitamin E, GMOD™ complex, glycerin"/>
<p>Power Peptide Micro Emulsion has a more targeted place: I use it sparingly around my forehead and nasolabial folds, and I’m careful with how much.</p>
<div class="figrow"><figure class="fig"><img src="/img/mel-peel-l.webp" alt="A hand holding a grey tube of Melumé Pro Strength Multi-Acid Micro Peel." loading="lazy"><figcaption>Micro Peel³ is an occasional step in my skincare.</figcaption></figure><figure class="fig"><img src="/img/mel-mask-l.webp" alt="A hand holding a dark-blue tube of Melumé Nightly Morphing Mask." loading="lazy"><figcaption>Nightly Morphing Mask, which I sometimes leave on overnight.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h2>A peel now and then, a mask sometimes</h2>
<p>What I love is the velvety feel afterwards.</p>
<p>The peel is at most about twice a month for me; my skin feels thin and soft, and I don’t feel the need to exfoliate more often. The Nightly Morphing Mask is the one in the dark-blue tube with a built-in brush. I leave it on overnight from time to time and love the glow I wake up to. On its product page, Melumé <a href="https://www.melume-skinscience.com/products/overnight-face-mask" target="_blank" rel="noopener">lists it as a retinal overnight mask</a>.</p>
<figure class="fig"><img src="/img/mel-cleanser-l.webp" alt="A hand holding a white tube of Melumé Balmy Oily Milky Cleanser." loading="lazy"><figcaption>The cleansing balm I choose for a slower skincare ritual.</figcaption></figure>
<h2>The cleansing balm</h2>
<p>When I want a slower ritual.</p>
<p>I usually prefer creamy or foaming textures for everyday cleansing. I reach for the balm when I want the cleansing step itself to feel a little more luxurious.</p>
<h2>Also on my shelf</h2>
<p>Melanin Spot Eraser is a later addition, and it wasn’t part of the twelve-product video. I apply a small amount to areas of pigmentation when I want targeted care, and I noticed my husband’s post-acne marks looking lighter when he used it. My mum has her own favourites from the brand: Power Peptide Micro Emulsion, Nightly Morphing Mask and Super C-Cream.</p>
<h2>Where I’d start</h2>
<p>For my normal-to-dry skin, I would start again with Hydrating Serum 8HA, Hydrating Cream 8HA and the lip balm. They’re the ones I use most consistently and keep finishing; the others have a place when I want something more specific.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jpk-JUTkHbE" target="_blank" rel="noopener">My full Melumé video</a> shows the products and their textures. It was filmed as a presentation of the wider line, so the “let’s begin our routine” at the start isn’t a prescribed full routine.</p>
<ul>
<li>Hydrating Serum 8HA Everyday, morning and evening</li>
<li>Hydrating Cream 8HA Throughout the year</li>
<li>Lip balm Throughout the day</li>
</ul>
